 "notes": "Table XV Part II (Bilingualism), one mother tongue per opening; rows = the same 48 areas as Part I (Agency, four sub-agencies, states). Only Males and Females printed (persons null); no printed column numbers (cols null). subsidiary=null records are 'Number of persons speaking Mother Tongue'. Area names follow the Part I files (printed here 'Junagadh', 'Chunda', 'Malek Shri Joravar Khan's State (Varahi)' -> Part I 'Junagad', 'Chuda', \"Malek Shri Joravarkhan's State (Varahi)\"). Nil cells ('..', '....') omitted. Print inconsistency: Two subsidiary languages, Females - A. Seventeen Salute States printed 7 (and Agency 12 = 7 + 5 consistent with it), but the states print Junagad 2 + Palanpur 6 = 8 (both re-read on zoom, clear); kept as printed. Two/three/four-subsidiary counts are not included in the Total subsidiary languages column (Total = sum of the individual subsidiary-language columns in every row)."
